    <ul>
    <li>Contains <strong>no one-way loop and no 30 km/h figure</strong> (searched: "one-way", "loop" other than bus loop services, "30 km/h").</li>
    <li>Raises, as options to consider (none tested): <q>Review of speed limits in high pedestrian areas and the possible adoption of lower speeds or shared traffic zones</q> in areas such as the CBD <a href="/n/sources-register#S-B04">[S-B04 p.70]</a>; <q>Signalisation of intersections</q> for safer pedestrian crossings <a href="/n/sources-register#S-B04">[S-B04 p.50]</a>; on Torrens St the <q>critical junctions with Seaview Road and Crozier Road</q> <a href="/n/sources-register#S-B04">[S-B04 p.52]</a>; and <q>Consideration of signalising roundabouts and the installation of traffic signals</q> as key east-west intersections reach capacity <a href="/n/sources-register#S-B04">[S-B04 p.71]</a>.</li>
